cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DuckVEP or Rduckvep, please cite the software and the accompanying preprint."
title: "DuckVEP: relation-first variant consequence and haplotype annotation in DuckDB"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Toure
    given-names: Sounkou Mahamane
    email: sounkoutoure@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/RGenomicsETL/DuckVEP"
url: "https://rgenomicsetl.github.io/DuckVEP/"
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - variant annotation
  - consequence prediction
  - haplotype
  - DuckDB
  - Ensembl VEP
abstract: >-
  DuckVEP is a DuckDB extension, and Rduckvep its R front end, for
  relation-first variant consequence and phased whole-haplotype annotation
  against Ensembl transcript models, with executable conformance against
  Ensembl VEP 116, bcftools csq, Haplosaurus and Mutalyzer.
